  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "All five completed experiments are singleprofile, so we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile (with aggregation) improves performance. The strongest finding is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l substantially outperforms scgpt-based configs (~0.53 vs ~0.42-0.43), and weighted fusion marginally edges concat for scvi_n200 (0.5375 vs 0.5321). Config_046 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the most direct multiprofile extension of our best singleprofile config (config_006), changing only the profile setting and adding the simplest aggregation (avgpool). This isolates the effect of multiprofile while holding the RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy constant. It is the highest-value next experiment because profile setting is the largest unexplored design axis, and knowing whether multiple profiles add signal (or just noise/complexity) will strongly guide all subsequent experiments involving aggregation and fusion."
}

